<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Álvaro Obregón</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1880">1880</a>–<a href="/years/1928">1928</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Álvaro Obregón was a Mexican general and president from 1920 to 1924. A leading Constitutionalist commander in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-revolution">Mexican Revolution</a>, he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pancho-villa">Pancho Villa</a> at the battles of Celaya in 1915 and came to power through the Agua Prieta revolt of 1920. Re-elected president in 1928, he was assassinated by a Catholic militant before taking office.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alvaro-obregon.jpg" alt="Álvaro Obregón" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harris &amp; Ewing · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Obreg%C3%B3n_Salido,_%C3%81lvaro_(cropped)(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
